ere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.4$ | $0.05$ | $0.45$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.55$ | $0.45$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, using the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y=2) & ={f}_{Y}(2) \\\\  & =f(1,2)+f(2,2)+f(3,2) \\\\  & =0.25+0.05+0.15 \\\\  & =0.45.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077246/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4aef7734bbc5730ab599539f284a667fc67e4f7632fb3d6586cf67de799a89"} {"question" "q-142562" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077246/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ab1426502a00d5f25d5107f364533e6c4ccbc0670f5384cfb1fd01c1a3a94048"} {"question" "q-142562" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077246/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4aef7734bbc5730ab599539f284a667fc67e4f7632fb3d6586cf67de799a89"} {"question" "q-142562" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.3"] ["math" "0.45"] ["math" "0.5"] ["math" "0.55"] ["math" "0.6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077246/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4aef7734bbc5730ab599539f284a667fc67e4f7632fb3d6586cf67de799a89"} {"question" "q-142562" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct