" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{9}{16}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ | $\\frac{7}{16}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{7}{16}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, using the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y=1) & ={f}_{Y}(1) \\\\  & =f(1,1)+f(2,1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077246/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4aef7734bbc5730ab599539f284a667fc67e4f7632fb3d6586cf67de799a89"} {"question" "q-142559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077246/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ab1426502a00d5f25d5107f364533e6c4ccbc0670f5384cfb1fd01c1a3a94048"} {"question" "q-142559" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077246/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4aef7734bbc5730ab599539f284a667fc67e4f7632fb3d6586cf67de799a89"} {"question" "q-142559" "field" "selection" "attribute" "ans