rginal mass function for $X$ is given in the following table:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.35$ | $0.45$ | $0.2$ |\n\nFinally, using the table of values of the marginal mass function for $X,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<2) & =P(X\\in {0,1}) \\\\  & =P(X=0)+P(X=1) \\\\  & =0.35+0.45 \\\\  & =0.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077246/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4aef7734bbc5730ab599539f284a667fc67e4f7632fb3d6586cf67de799a89"} {"question" "q-142572" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077246/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ab1426502a00d5f25d5107f364533e6c4ccbc0670f5384cfb1fd01c1a3a94048"} {"question" "q-142572" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077246/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4aef7734bbc5730ab599539f284a667fc67e4f7632fb3d6586cf67de799a89"} {"question" "q-142572" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.55"] ["math" "0.65"] ["math" "0.7"] ["math" "0.75"] ["math" "0.8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077246/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4aef7734bbc5730ab599539f284a667fc67e4f7632fb3d6586cf67de799a89"} {"question" "q-142572" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077246/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c4aef7734bbc5730ab599539f284a667fc67e4f7632fb3d6586cf67de799a89"} {"question" "q-142718" "field" nil "attribute" "question/p